Adapt test_builtin, test_descr, and test_module to run through normal unittest discovery on both interpreters.
Guard CPython-only imports and test setup, and remove methods whose syntax Monty cannot parse (generators, metaclasses, deletion of names or items, and unsupported class bodies).
Keep the builtin doctests in a named CPython test and require the main thread for PTY tests that install signal handlers.
Keep upstream dir() assertions where supported; guard probes for native module subclassing, slots, traceback attributes, object construction, direct __dir__ calls, and descriptors.
Give the CPython module shutdown subprocess access to the pinned test package.

